{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"I don’t have the bank’s reviewed agreements here, so I can’t confirm its specific findings. Generally:\n\n- **Cash collateral:** An AP delivering securities late may have to post additional cash—for example, **115%**, where the governing documents specify that rate.\n- **Valuation base:** The percentage applies to the **market value of the undelivered securities**, not the entire creation basket or the ETF shares’ NAV. Mark-to-market adjustments may require top-ups.\n\n**Worth knowing:** This is **not a universal rate** across US ETFs. The applicable percentage, valuation timing and collateral requirements depend on the particular fund’s AP agreement and related governing documents."}}
